From: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: provide the multi-gig link speeds

QSDK kernels extend enum switch_port_speed with 2.5G/5G/10G, mainline
does not.  Define the missing values locally.

Signed-off-by: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
---
--- a/src/ref/ref_port_ctrl.c	2026-07-20 11:22:55.000000000 +0800
+++ b/src/ref/ref_port_ctrl.c	2026-11-21 10:41:56.525230145 +0800
@@ -37,6 +37,17 @@
 #include <linux/time.h>
 #include "ref_port_ctrl.h"
 
+/* QSDK kernels extend enum switch_port_speed with the multi-gig rates */
+#ifndef SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_2500
+#define SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_2500 2500
+#endif
+#ifndef SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_5000
+#define SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_5000 5000
+#endif
+#ifndef SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_10000
+#define SWITCH_PORT_SPEED_10000 10000
+#endif
+
 #if defined(IN_SWCONFIG)
 int qca_ar8327_sw_get_port_link(struct switch_dev *dev, int port,
 	struct switch_port_link *link)
